    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b8356a3_95696f87",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010077
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-22T10:11:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "E.g. -include-runtime might not be the best idea to allow on Android, -X flags are experimental and subject to change. Anyway, gradle (and AFAIK bazel and buck) wrap support in their DSL, so e.g. treating warnings as errors in gradle is accomplished by:\n\n compileKotlin {\n    kotlinOptions.allWarningsAsErrors \u003d true\n }\n\nand trying out coroutines looks something like this:\n\n  kotlin {\n    experimental {\n        coroutines \u0027enable\u0027\n    }\n  }\n\n\n\nI think I agree with the idea of adding support for certain features incrementally rather than opening the gates for all and then chase the ones to remove.\n\nIn fact, I\u0027d like to see a way to add support for plugins like kapt and android extensions done in a similar fashion. I think support from Jetbrains would be needed for that to go smoother.",
      "parentUuid": "4b9230fb_2b9bee2d",
      "revId": "4ed1659ed0bede8dd77850c80b7db17d8c3614a9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
