        "uuid": "c98db474_96a63f12",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010077
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-22T10:11:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From what I hear, coroutines are in fact stabilized from kotlin 1.3. Not sure what the flags look like there, haven\u0027t tried 1.3 yet. On the other hand, it\u0027s one of the most sought for features among my colleagues to have until 1.3 stable release.",
      "parentUuid": "d3c40da0_65ca61e2",
      "revId": "4ed1659ed0bede8dd77850c80b7db17d8c3614a9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae08b5d3_2bdb54b8",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-11T20:46:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to https://blog.jetbrains.com/kotlin/2018/07/see-whats-coming-in-kotlin-1-3-m1/, code using experimental coroutines will not compile in 1.3, so I think this should wait until 1.3 is available, at which point it probably won\u0027t even need the -Xcoroutines flag.",
      "parentUuid": "c98db474_96a63f12",
      "revId": "4ed1659ed0bede8dd77850c80b7db17d8c3614a9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c06990a_89949957",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010077
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-12T14:45:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On that page it also says: \"we’ll add a compatibility layer in 1.3 and the classes for experimental coroutines will still remain in the standard library. The compiled Kotlin/JVM code that uses experimental coroutines from 1.1 or 1.2 would still continue to work in Kotlin 1.3.\"\nSo we need to worry about later versions.\n\nAnyway, with this implementation gone in favor of list of flags, it doesn\u0027t really matter.",
      "parentUuid": "ae08b5d3_2bdb54b8",
      "revId": "4ed1659ed0bede8dd77850c80b7db17d8c3614a9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
