      },
      "lineNbr": 1319,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010077
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-22T10:11:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t disagree. Not sure how consistent the use of -Werror is, though. Maybe going with compiler\u0027s defaults is sane in this case? Sounds reasonable to list warnings and then use switches to either not show them at all (-no-warn) or treat them as errors (-Werror). Mind you, this implementation would not allow ignoring warnings, but warning suppression should be trivial to add this way.",
      "parentUuid": "1eaa0162_9d8a010f",
      "revId": "4ed1659ed0bede8dd77850c80b7db17d8c3614a9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
